This MIT License applies to the original code, documentation, schema,
examples, and project-authored sample records in this repository.

Source texts, translations, and older scholarly materials referenced or
excerpted in the sample data may have different copyright status depending
on jurisdiction; verify before reuse.

Materials referenced in the sample data include Homer's Iliad in A.T.
Murray's 1924 translation (via the Perseus Digital Library), Seneca's
Epistulae Morales in Richard M. Gummere's 1917 Loeb edition, and Plato's
Republic in Benjamin Jowett's 1871 translation (via Project Gutenberg).
These older translations and commentaries are commonly treated as public
domain in the United States, but status can vary by jurisdiction.
